  "source_review": "All six complete C and native bodies inspected. The scheduler has genuine no-input global-context helpers and live later-row activity, with result-byte narrowing. Small insertion preserves ascending strict-less order; large insertion preserves the head anchor and its different comparison, including group creation before pool exhaustion. Mixed ABI is one object pointer plus five actual floats. Initializer matches precise packed416-byte and aligned40-byte writes, including untouched bytes and native-aligned words40. Group insertion retains the pre-unlink low-byte slot and pointer while reloading live group state; unchanged-channel early exit is preserved. Synchronized controller pair keeps both real components, channel reload and one matching synchronization exit. No artificial source or ABI blocker found.",
  "qualification": "Final README explicitly retains the valid allocated lists and32-entry unchecked small-pool capacity, N64-only pointer widths, mandatory large-list head anchor and ordinary FP-state/quiet-NaN limitations. These match the inspected native behavior; no semantic blocker.",
